A||||6||fieroX||my fiero vs 2001 crown vic||||8||
Z||000000||fieroX||11-08-2001||02:33 PM||||so last night im heading out to my dads house for dinner, and on the way I get caught up in some traffic.  so im sitting at the back of a line of traffic watching my rearview for some space to take the right lane, around about 15 cars.  Finally all the cars are clear so I dart over into the right lane and just as I pull beside the guy that was directly in front of me, he decides to take the right lane also.  BOOM, pushes me into the curb at about 20 mph and a 30 degree angle.  He pulls ahead of me and gets out too see if im ok, and I do the same.  I looked at my car and nothing happened on the driver side.  I have a small scuff of paint on my mirror, and a small scuff on my door trim.  I popped my passenger tire though, and messed up the rim pretty good.  His passenger side front door is jacked up real good.  Thank god for plastic cars.  My driver side window is harder to roll up and down now though.  <BR>The part that sucks the most, is the cop that came out said it was nobodys fault because we were both doing the same thing.  He was some disabled vet, and I think he got a sympathy thing going on with the cop, because im just a 21 year old kid with a sports car.  Oh well, at least Im only out a tire, and I need front tires before the winter anyway.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||11-08-2001||02:37 PM||||Man that sucks! I feel your pain!(Bill Clinton Laugh)<P>If you hit the curb hard enough to pop a tire and screw up a rim you probably have more damage then you think. Get your bearings checked, tie rods could be bent, rack could be screwed up, you probably need an alignment also.<P>Good luck!<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000002||fieroX||11-08-2001||03:11 PM||||what sucks more is that just the day before I paid 85 bucks for a 4 wheel alignment.  I dont care now.  Mabye its messed up maybe not.  Ill get it realigned when I get my 17's on there in the spring, and im putting in all new poly bushings etc.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Huck||11-08-2001||05:18 PM||||Fiero's are tanks Im tellin ya!  A lot of people think that they are death traps and would fold like paper in an accident, but I've had 3 encounters with other vehicles in the past years.  I was the victor in all 3 accidents.  <P>97 honda civic backed into (and OVER my front end!) dented their plastic bumper up good, scuffed the paint a little on the fiero.<P>87 dodge caravan - I T-boned it when he ran a stop sign.  nailed the sliding door real good, and apparently bent the frame.  fiero's head lights didnt go down, and the front clip popped off its mounts.  bent something with a crowbar, popped the clip back on, and I was on my way, with the only noticable problem again being some chipped paint.<P>80 mustang -  rear ended me and wrote off the front end of his car  all I had was some broken tail light lenses and again some scratched paint...<P>Maybe I've just been lucky, I dunno.. the only thing that crushed me so far has been a 2001 chev Z71 .. the damn things trailer hitch went right up my hood when he backed into me...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||11-08-2001||07:02 PM||||If your window is harder to roll up, then you've tweeked the frame. If you're lucky it's just the door... Does it still open/close properly? That's a good way to check for frame damage...<P>Oh, and the cop's wrong... You were established in the lane, and in his blind-spot. He's responsible for shoulder-checking before making a lane-change manouver. If he didn't have his signal on, even more to ya... <P>Good luck.||||reg||4
Z||000005||fieroX||11-08-2001||09:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>If your window is harder to roll up, then you've tweeked the frame. If you're lucky it's just the door... Does it still open/close properly? That's a good way to check for frame damage...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the door open and closes just like it used to.  I dont even think the alignment is off, just pissed me off this guy is trying to take me out before my project has really started.  If I had my rims on there Id be really mad right now, im not so worried about the original 14's.  <BR>Im not taking it to court or anything even though I think the cop was wrong.  It would cost me more in court fees and lawyer fees than I would get for a scuffed mirror and a popped tire.  No biggy, just on with the project.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||btoth||11-08-2001||11:33 PM||||Even if the cop was wrong.  If something <I>is</I> seriously messed up with your car that you didn't notice at first, your insurance can deal with it.<P>When my car was totaled, the cop found no-one at fault, but the insurance saw differently.  They convinced the other driver's insurance company that he was the one that screwed up.||||reg||1
